{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"TITLE:\"Multilayer DNA origami packed on hexagonal and hybrid lattices\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"22187940","source":"MED","pmid":"22187940","pmcid":"PMC3336742","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC3336742"]},"doi":"10.1021/ja209719k","title":"Multilayer DNA origami packed on hexagonal and hybrid lattices.","authorString":"Ke Y, Voigt NV, Gothelf KV, Shih WM.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Ke Y","firstName":"Yonggang","lastName":"Ke","initials":"Y","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1673-2153"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Cancer Biology, Dana-Farber Cancer Institute, and Department of Biological Chemistry and Molecular Pharmacology, Harvard Medical School, Boston, Massachusetts 02115, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Voigt NV","firstName":"Niels V","lastName":"Voigt","initials":"NV"},{"fullName":"Gothelf KV","firstName":"Kurt V","lastName":"Gothelf","initials":"KV"},{"fullName":"Shih WM","firstName":"William M","lastName":"Shih","initials":"WM"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1673-2153"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"134","journalIssueId":1899515,"dateOfPublication":"2012 Jan","monthOfPublication":1,"yearOfPublication":2012,"printPublicationDate":"2012-01-01","journal":{"title":"Journal of the American Chemical Society","medlineAbbreviation":"J Am Chem Soc","isoabbreviation":"J Am Chem Soc","essn":"1520-5126","issn":"0002-7863","nlmid":"7503056"}},"pubYear":"2012","pageInfo":"1770-1774","abstractText":"\"Scaffolded DNA origami\" has been proven to be a powerful and efficient approach to construct two-dimensional or three-dimensional objects with great complexity. Multilayer DNA origami has been demonstrated with helices packing along either honeycomb-lattice geometry or square-lattice geometry. Here we report successful folding of multilayer DNA origami with helices arranged on a close-packed hexagonal lattice. This arrangement yields a higher density of helical packing and therefore higher resolution of spatial addressing than has been shown previously. We also demonstrate hybrid multilayer DNA origami with honeycomb-lattice, square-lattice, and hexagonal-lattice packing of helices all in one design. The availability of hexagonal close-packing of helices extends our ability to build complex structures using DNA nanotechnology.","affiliation":"Department of Cancer Biology, Dana-Farber Cancer Institute, and Department of Biological Chemistry and Molecular Pharmacology, Harvard Medical School, Boston, Massachusetts 02115, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Research Support, U.S. Gov't, Non-P.H.S.","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"grantId":"1DP2OD004641-01","agency":"NIH HHS","acronym":"OD","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"DP2 OD004641","agency":"NIH HHS","acronym":"OD","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"DNA","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Nucleic Acid Conformation"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Nanotechnology","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Models, Molecular"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Nanostructures","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"UL","qualifierName":"ultrastructure","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"DNA","registryNumber":"9007-49-2"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Me